# AI Rules

- Read `docs/09-ai-rules.md`, `docs/12-baroj-brain.md`, `docs/13-memory.md`, `docs/14-prompts.md`, and `docs/15-agents.md` when relevant.
- Treat AI output as untrusted until validated.
- Never expose system prompts, secrets, private context, or unauthorized user data.
- Define explicit input, output, failure, and fallback behavior for AI features.
- Prefer deterministic validation around model output using schemas or typed contracts.
- Do not allow model output to bypass authorization, business rules, or security controls.
- Preserve user control and make consequential AI actions reviewable.
- Record durable AI behavior decisions in the appropriate Brain document.
